acb@yoyo.cc.monash.edu.au (Andrew Bulhak) writes:

> It's time to put away once and for all the illusion that the EFF are
> some kind of heroic freedom fighters, opposing the forces of oppression.
> The EFF is a good dog who knows his master. They did nothing about AA...

It would have been foolish for EFF to focus their efforts on preventing an
initial conviction in the AA BBS case.  Preventing that conviction
wouldn't have set a precedent disallowing the tactics used by government
in the case.  Getting the conviction overturned on a subsequent appeal
might set that precedent, and is therefore much more in line with the
organization's mandate.  (As has been pointed out before, they're not a
"legal defense fund" -- if you want to see one, start one.)

If EFF refuses to involve themselves in the appeal, then you might have a 
case.  At the moment, you don't.

